WEBVTT

00:09.480 --> 00:14.910
<b>Saving 80,000 Gold
in Another World 
for My Retirement</b>

01:29.980 --> 01:32.980
The Adventure of Mitsuha

01:52.450 --> 01:54.300
So cute...

01:54.300 --> 01:58.290
<i>She may be a mercenary, 
but she's still got a girlish side to her...</i>

02:01.290 --> 02:03.260
Sorry for making you wait.

02:08.450 --> 02:10.650
That sure took you a while.

02:11.080 --> 02:13.690
You just went to hand him over 
and collect the bounty, didn't you?

02:13.690 --> 02:18.560
It seems there's been an uptick lately 
of shady fellows here in the royal capital.

02:18.560 --> 02:22.580
Which is why they make a fuss about 
background checks and the like.

02:23.580 --> 02:27.410
If you're going to live here alone, 
you should be careful, little lady.

02:28.180 --> 02:30.300
Thank you for the warning.

02:31.820 --> 02:34.680
<i>I'm well-prepared, though.</i>

02:37.060 --> 02:39.550
Please, have some tea while it's still hot.

02:39.940 --> 02:43.260
What a strange-looking tea... 
And this smell...

02:43.590 --> 02:45.220
It's called green tea.

02:45.220 --> 02:47.140
I hope you enjoy it.

02:50.540 --> 02:52.650
Ah... it's good!

02:53.060 --> 02:55.190
We haven't introduced ourselves yet.

02:55.190 --> 02:59.420
I'm Sven, the leader of this party.

02:59.420 --> 03:01.500
Ah, nice to meet you!

03:01.500 --> 03:03.310
Everyone else, go on.

03:03.310 --> 03:04.120
I'm Sepp.

03:04.610 --> 03:07.430
The name's Grit, and this is...

03:08.180 --> 03:09.440
Ilse...

03:09.440 --> 03:11.030
She's a little shy.

03:11.030 --> 03:14.540
Er... you wouldn't secretly 
happen to be a mage, would you?

03:15.740 --> 03:18.600
<i>I figured it'd follow after a swordsman, 
spearman, and warrior woman...</i>

03:18.600 --> 03:20.670
<i>but guess not!</i>

03:21.290 --> 03:24.500
So what's this mission you have for us?

03:24.500 --> 03:30.280
Right. I'd like to accompany you 
the next time you go out to hunt or forage.

03:30.280 --> 03:35.190
So could I ask you to act as my 
bodyguards and support during that time?

03:37.840 --> 03:41.290
I was hoping to stock items

03:41.290 --> 03:44.840
that would be useful for folks 
in your line of business,

03:45.450 --> 03:49.660
and thought it'd be best to go out there 
and see for myself for research purposes.

03:50.640 --> 03:52.920
Give us some time to talk it over.

03:52.920 --> 03:53.920
Go ahead.

03:56.100 --> 03:57.000
What should we do?

03:57.000 --> 03:59.350
A child like her as our client, huh?

03:59.350 --> 04:02.130
She may be a child, 
but she's a bona-fide shopkeeper!

04:02.860 --> 04:05.980
Wasn't our next destination 
a forest that's not too dangerous?

04:05.980 --> 04:08.670
I don't see much of a downside here.

04:08.670 --> 04:11.210
And it's not for hunting game, which means...

04:11.210 --> 04:14.100
We're guaranteed a retainer fee.

04:19.700 --> 04:21.440
We'll take on your request.

04:21.440 --> 04:23.240
Pleasure doing business with you!

04:23.240 --> 04:25.770
We plan on setting out next in two days.

04:25.770 --> 04:27.120
That works for me!

04:28.850 --> 04:31.580
I can smell the money already!

04:33.000 --> 04:34.830
<b>Hardware Store</b>

04:33.000 --> 04:34.830
<b>Theater</b>

04:34.210 --> 04:36.500
WcDonald's

04:50.010 --> 04:52.340
I'll be borrowing these for a bit, Onii-chan.

04:52.340 --> 04:53.620
No problem!

04:53.620 --> 04:55.250
Keep your tail raised!

04:55.250 --> 04:56.520
Okay!

05:02.450 --> 05:04.860
We're here way earlier 
than the scheduled time.

05:04.860 --> 05:08.120
Well, we can't keep 
a client waiting, now can we?

05:08.560 --> 05:10.490
Wait... she's already here?!

05:10.490 --> 05:12.080
Good morning!

05:12.080 --> 05:15.790
<i>This little lady must have been 
real excited for this!</i>

05:16.300 --> 05:20.680
<i>What's the deal with her strange 
clothes and all that gear?!</i>

05:22.120 --> 05:26.720
<i>Well, it's a hundred times better than
if she'd shown up in a fancy, frilly dress...</i>

05:27.180 --> 05:29.430
Okay, let us be off!

05:29.890 --> 05:31.640
Y-Yeah...

05:45.420 --> 05:48.790
<i>This little lady's tougher 
than I'd taken her for.</i>

05:55.190 --> 05:58.430
Excuse me. If I may ask a random question...

05:58.430 --> 06:00.310
Hmm? What is it?

06:00.310 --> 06:02.290
How has your work been going lately?

06:02.290 --> 06:05.790
Things have been calm and 
peaceful lately in these parts.

06:05.790 --> 06:08.140
So business has been tough 
for mercenaries like us.

06:08.730 --> 06:11.260
I hear some have even taken to banditry.

06:11.780 --> 06:17.150
We've been scraping by honestly 
with odd jobs and hunting...

06:17.150 --> 06:18.560
But quite frankly...

06:19.240 --> 06:23.190
The pay's not great, so we have to be frugal.

06:23.190 --> 06:26.550
Which is why we're really grateful 
for your request today.

06:27.070 --> 06:28.900
We'll work as hard as we can.

06:28.900 --> 06:32.130
Oh, no, I should be the one thanking you!

06:37.030 --> 06:39.750
Okay, let's leave our belongings here.

06:39.750 --> 06:41.990
<i>So this is our base camp.</i>

06:41.990 --> 06:43.590
What's on the agenda for today?

06:43.910 --> 06:48.510
First, we'll gather medicinal herbs and 
wild plants that'll fetch high prices.

06:49.050 --> 06:50.760
<i>Does he mean like wild yams?</i>

06:50.760 --> 06:53.160
<i>Digging those up sounds like a pain...</i>

06:53.160 --> 06:57.820
Er... then, Grit, do you mind 
if I tag along with you?

06:57.820 --> 06:59.440
Oh, be my guest.

07:02.450 --> 07:06.020
<i>When she digs up wild yams, 
I'll whip out some useful items!</i>

07:11.700 --> 07:15.160
<i>No wild yams in sight. Too bad.</i>

07:15.920 --> 07:19.320
We've gathered quite a bit. Let's head back.

07:19.320 --> 07:22.120
You should have left your gear at camp 
if you weren't going to use it.

07:22.120 --> 07:25.150
Ah, no, please don't worry about me.

07:25.150 --> 07:27.710
<i>To be honest, it's a little heavy...</i>

07:29.560 --> 07:31.260
Oh, you're back.

07:31.260 --> 07:33.610
Let's set up our bunks, then.

07:33.610 --> 07:34.610
You got it!

07:39.060 --> 07:40.520
There we go...

07:48.850 --> 07:50.470
Okay, that does it!

07:51.490 --> 07:53.860
Um... what if it rains?

07:54.460 --> 07:57.310
It's clear as it gets! 
I'm sure it won't rain!

07:57.310 --> 07:58.650
We'll be fine!

07:59.580 --> 08:01.580
Then, I'll be using this.

08:04.710 --> 08:06.220
Da-da-da-dun da-dun!

08:06.220 --> 08:08.170
Anywhere Tent!

08:08.170 --> 08:09.110
Wh-Wha?!

08:09.110 --> 08:10.460
What is <i>that</i>?!

08:10.910 --> 08:12.970
Insulation Mat!

08:13.340 --> 08:15.340
Wh-What in the world?!

08:15.340 --> 08:19.050
So... do you think these would sell?

08:19.050 --> 08:21.890
Y-Yeah... probably...

08:24.230 --> 08:25.830
You're making soup?

08:25.830 --> 08:26.740
Yep.

08:26.740 --> 08:27.480
Is it good?

08:28.720 --> 08:30.810
It's kind of bitter and gross.

08:30.810 --> 08:33.480
B-But it's edible, at the very least.

08:35.660 --> 08:38.100
Hmm, it's not lighting.

08:38.100 --> 08:40.730
The grass is a little damp.

08:41.590 --> 08:44.980
Er, do you mind if I try instead?

08:44.980 --> 08:46.750
Go ahead, give it a shot.

08:46.750 --> 08:49.200
It's okay, I brought my own.

08:50.090 --> 08:52.050
<b>Ignite-O
Camping Firestarter
For outdoor campfires, barbecues, and more{black text bottom}</b>

08:55.340 --> 08:57.180
Wh-What?!

08:58.700 --> 09:00.720
Science has triumphed!

09:04.730 --> 09:08.440
<b>Domestic
White Peaches
Quartered</b>

09:04.730 --> 09:08.440
<b>Smooth Red Bean Paste</b>

09:09.420 --> 09:12.690
The rest of your luggage is all food?!

09:13.420 --> 09:18.410
Oh, I brought too much to eat alone, 
so could you help me out?

09:18.410 --> 09:22.330
In exchange, I'd like you to 
sample some of these foods here.

09:23.220 --> 09:26.290
S-Sure. I don't mind.

09:26.290 --> 09:29.250
Here, this is minestrone.

09:33.340 --> 09:35.330
Huh? It's good!

09:35.670 --> 09:39.170
When'd you have time to 
make this, little lady?

09:39.170 --> 09:41.680
You could open a high-class 
restaurant with those skills!

09:41.680 --> 09:44.470
<i>Too bad! I bought this 
in a can at the supermarket!</i>

09:44.980 --> 09:48.190
What is this, bread? It's so soft!

09:48.190 --> 09:50.440
And what's this sweet stuff inside?

09:50.440 --> 09:55.070
<i>Sorry to disappoint. This is anpan 
that sells for 148 yen per 5-pack.</i>

09:55.070 --> 09:58.580
If only she weren't a child, 
I'd ask her out on a date...

09:58.580 --> 10:00.490
<i>I'm not a child, but okay.</i>

10:00.880 --> 10:02.750
Do you think I could sell these?

10:02.750 --> 10:06.030
Other than the bread, 
they'll all keep for a while.

10:06.870 --> 10:08.560
Hmm, depends on the prices.

10:08.560 --> 10:11.990
But even if it's pricey, I'm sure 
aristocrats and other rich people,

10:11.990 --> 10:14.710
as well as the military, would buy it all up.

10:15.130 --> 10:16.700
I see...

10:16.700 --> 10:18.150
<i>The military, huh?</i>

10:18.150 --> 10:19.260
Are you sure about that?

10:19.260 --> 10:21.890
Things can get messy when it 
comes to handling military goods.

10:21.890 --> 10:25.760
You'll have to deal with all sorts of weird 
requests, and if you show weakness...

10:25.760 --> 10:27.600
Well, I'll worry about it then!

10:27.600 --> 10:28.970
I understand.

10:28.970 --> 10:31.020
Aristocrats and military aside,

10:31.020 --> 10:35.010
I'll do my best to set prices so that 
people like you can easily afford them!

10:35.010 --> 10:37.470
Huh? Are you out of your mind, young lady?!

10:37.470 --> 10:39.610
If you played it right, 
you could make a fortune!

10:39.610 --> 10:43.640
That's fine. I can make my 
profit from other products.

10:44.100 --> 10:45.080
<i>Hmm?</i>

10:45.080 --> 10:48.710
<i>Huh? They all look so deeply moved.</i>

10:48.710 --> 10:50.540
<i>Was it that delicious?</i>

10:50.540 --> 10:53.380
I also have some tea as an 
after-dinner drink, if you'd like.

10:53.380 --> 10:55.250
Yes, gladly!

10:55.250 --> 10:56.940
<i>What is this, an izakaya?</i>

10:57.340 --> 11:00.300
Fragrant, Traditional
 Royal Palace Black Tea
 Royal Milk Tea

11:03.330 --> 11:07.230
Well, then... 
I'm off to go get ready for bed.

11:19.180 --> 11:22.790
<i>I'm glad I prepared this to wash up in.</i>

11:22.790 --> 11:25.250
<i>I ended up sweating buckets today.</i>

11:28.040 --> 11:30.370
Y-Young lady! You... You...

11:30.870 --> 11:33.300
You clod! Just look at you!

11:33.300 --> 11:34.220
Huh?

11:34.850 --> 11:37.210
Look the other way, men!

11:37.210 --> 11:38.790
What are you thinking,

11:38.790 --> 11:41.010
coming out naked in front of these men?!

11:41.010 --> 11:43.280
Ah, no, this is a swimsuit, 
and it's fine to show...

11:43.280 --> 11:46.510
Quiet, you! That doesn't 
even count as underwear!

11:46.510 --> 11:48.520
Practically naked...

11:49.590 --> 11:53.170
<i>Ah, looks like I've messed up again...</i>

11:56.160 --> 12:02.600
<i>And after a long lecture, I was 
finally allowed to take a bath...</i>

12:03.390 --> 12:05.930
Grit, would you like to join me?

12:05.930 --> 12:07.990
I won't be so shameless as you!

12:08.430 --> 12:11.280
<i>She totally thinks I'm a sicko!</i>

12:11.960 --> 12:14.960
<b>Saving 80,000 Gold in
Another World 
for My Retirement</b>

12:14.960 --> 12:17.970
<b>Saving 80,000 Gold in
Another World 
for My Retirement</b>

12:18.370 --> 12:21.010
<i>Dun da-da-dun da-da-dun!</i>

12:21.670 --> 12:23.630
Plain

12:21.670 --> 12:23.630
Nutritionally
balanced food{white on black, 1st from left}

12:21.670 --> 12:23.630
8 kinds
of vitamins
Niacin,
Folic acid

12:21.670 --> 12:23.630
Calcium,
Iron

12:21.670 --> 12:23.630
Plenty of
dietary fiber

12:21.670 --> 12:23.630
2-bar pouches

12:21.670 --> 12:23.630
4 bars in 2 pouches

12:24.690 --> 12:26.600
What do you think about this food?

12:26.600 --> 12:28.120
It's good.

12:28.120 --> 12:31.350
It's not much, but I feel 
energized from eating it.

12:31.350 --> 12:33.810
<i>Okay, pretty good reviews.</i>

12:34.220 --> 12:36.190
We'll be off once we're done eating.

12:37.900 --> 12:40.230
<i>I'm gettin' excited!</i>

12:44.910 --> 12:47.370
<i>Now we're talking!</i>

12:50.830 --> 12:52.900
<i>Okay... happy hunting!</i>

12:52.900 --> 12:55.710
Okay... happy hunting, Mitsuha!

12:56.580 --> 13:00.400
For a hunt, everyone has their own style 
of attacking, their own attack range,

13:00.400 --> 13:03.590
and compatibility based on the prey.

13:03.590 --> 13:07.840
And often, one person alone is 
not enough to take down big game.

13:08.470 --> 13:11.670
That's why it's reassuring 
to tackle it as a team.

13:12.900 --> 13:13.850
<i>A bird!</i>

13:15.930 --> 13:17.970
<i>How are Ilse's skills?</i>

13:20.540 --> 13:21.580
Sorry...

13:21.580 --> 13:23.110
You almost had it!

13:26.400 --> 13:27.240
<i>Ah!</i>

13:28.740 --> 13:29.740
<i>A bird!</i>

13:30.150 --> 13:32.330
Sven, I see a bird.

13:33.430 --> 13:34.150
Ilse.

13:34.150 --> 13:38.170
Wait, let me have a shot at it.

13:38.170 --> 13:41.610
<i>Bows don't have that high 
of an accuracy to begin with...</i>

13:41.610 --> 13:42.420
<i>And what's more...</i>

13:42.420 --> 13:46.260
<i>The conditions are bad from this 
angle, with foliage in the way...</i>

13:47.300 --> 13:49.220
<i>It'd be difficult even for Ilse.</i>

13:51.130 --> 13:52.740
<i>It's a request from our employer.</i>

13:52.740 --> 13:54.680
<i>I suppose it's fine if we let one go.</i>

13:54.680 --> 13:56.860
Okay, give it a shot.

13:57.460 --> 13:58.950
Thank you very much.

14:06.290 --> 14:07.360
Incredible...

14:07.360 --> 14:10.070
<i>I did it! I did it, Captain!</i>

14:11.620 --> 14:14.680
<i>In fact, I was trained 
in the crossbow, as well!</i>

14:15.990 --> 14:19.080
That one's for sale. Not for us to eat!

14:19.080 --> 14:20.470
Mm-hmm.

14:20.470 --> 14:23.180
<i>He sure is reliable as their leader!</i>

14:24.090 --> 14:26.280
It's about time we returned to the capital.

14:27.930 --> 14:30.130
Well? Did you have fun?

14:30.130 --> 14:32.970
Yes! It was all so much fun!

14:34.350 --> 14:37.930
Er, I... need to answer nature's call...

14:38.330 --> 14:41.200
Hmm? Picking more plants?

14:41.200 --> 14:42.320
I'll come with you.

14:42.940 --> 14:45.370
It's fine, go by yourself.

14:45.370 --> 14:46.400
Yes!

14:46.960 --> 14:48.860
<i>Bathroom, bathroom...</i>

14:48.860 --> 14:52.820
<i>Thing would get messy if I jumped 
back home and they found out...</i>

14:52.820 --> 14:54.780
<i>Okay, around here should do.</i>

14:54.780 --> 14:56.750
<i>I said "do", not "doo".</i>

14:56.750 --> 14:58.280
<i>I'm here to pee.</i>

15:01.960 --> 15:03.590
A boar?!

15:03.590 --> 15:05.010
<i>Did I invade its territory?</i>

15:05.010 --> 15:06.550
<i>Or am I its prey?</i>

15:07.040 --> 15:10.210
<i>No, I'm supposed to be the hunter here!</i>

15:12.290 --> 15:15.430
<i>At times like these, 
there's only one path to take!</i>

15:15.430 --> 15:17.240
<i>Run away!</i>

15:18.180 --> 15:20.150
<i>Boars can't turn very quickly!</i>

15:21.780 --> 15:23.980
<i>No, it's right behind me!</i>

15:23.980 --> 15:26.570
<i>It's no use... I feel like I'm going to trip!</i>

15:32.650 --> 15:33.530
<i>No way!</i>

15:36.100 --> 15:37.490
I-I'm out of bullets?

15:37.490 --> 15:39.630
I'm dead!

15:40.460 --> 15:42.610
I know, I'll jum—

15:47.120 --> 15:49.050
I'm saved!

15:49.610 --> 15:53.270
<i>Maybe 9mm rounds are a little 
too weak against animals...</i>

15:53.720 --> 15:55.570
What's wrong?! What happened?!

15:55.570 --> 15:57.850
Oh, no! They'll find out about the gun!

15:58.230 --> 16:00.480
<i>Sorry, this might be overkill...</i>

16:02.190 --> 16:03.810
Eh?!

16:03.810 --> 16:04.600
Ah...

16:04.600 --> 16:08.190
It suddenly jumped out at me, but it 
worked out when I shot it in panic...

16:11.510 --> 16:14.220
Er, is something wrong?

16:14.220 --> 16:17.450
There wasn't any sound when you shot the bird.

16:17.450 --> 16:19.280
Huh, is that right?

16:19.280 --> 16:21.240
Maybe you're hearing things!

16:24.370 --> 16:26.940
We protect our clients' secrets!

16:26.940 --> 16:29.800
That's the code that we mercenaries live by!

16:31.870 --> 16:34.500
<i>That concludes this adventure!</i>

16:35.100 --> 16:39.400
<i>Well, we didn't get an event where 
we fight a dragon or anything.</i>

16:39.400 --> 16:40.600
<i>What a shame!</i>

16:45.400 --> 16:46.880
It's Mitsuha!

16:46.880 --> 16:48.540
Mitsuha!

16:52.610 --> 16:55.110
Good work, everyone!

16:58.660 --> 17:01.140
Our expedition was a rousing success!

17:01.140 --> 17:02.620
Makes the ale taste better!

17:03.860 --> 17:07.190
We got lots of birds and 
animals to sell for a good price.

17:07.190 --> 17:09.670
We can live off all this for half a month...

17:10.690 --> 17:13.550
And we received a gold coin on top,

17:13.550 --> 17:17.010
as well as a flattering review 
to the mercenary guild...

17:17.010 --> 17:19.050
I really don't know how 
we can ever thank you.

17:19.050 --> 17:21.800
No, the pleasure's all mine!

17:21.800 --> 17:24.270
<i>They don't pry into the private 
lives of their clients...</i>

17:24.270 --> 17:27.770
<i>Sven and the others were 
mercenaries of honor...</i>

17:27.770 --> 17:32.600
<i>Besides, I got to do 
tons of product research.</i>

17:33.740 --> 17:36.320
Hey, is that fire-lighting stick expensive?

17:36.850 --> 17:38.990
It really doesn't cost that much.

17:38.990 --> 17:41.670
For a smaller, different type,

17:41.670 --> 17:45.040
you can use it hundreds of times 
and it costs less than one silver.

17:45.040 --> 17:46.160
What?!

17:47.330 --> 17:50.550
Huh? You two don't sound surprised.

17:50.550 --> 17:53.380
Cooking's none of our business.

17:53.770 --> 17:54.840
I see...

17:55.560 --> 17:58.640
<i>It's none of the men's business? Is that so?!</i>

17:59.090 --> 18:00.550
Ah, I almost forgot!

18:01.010 --> 18:02.970
Take a look at this!

18:04.180 --> 18:06.850
<b>Momomi Tawawa</b>

18:04.180 --> 18:06.850
<b>A gravure mag favorite!
A killer bod exploding with energy!</b>

18:04.180 --> 18:06.850
Extra special feature! Jiggling and bursting at the seams!

18:08.850 --> 18:11.500
<i>When I went back to put away my luggage,</i>

18:11.500 --> 18:13.820
<i>I also brought this back 
with me from my world!</i>

18:14.490 --> 18:19.450
You really treated me like I was 
a loony for wearing that swimsuit!

18:19.800 --> 18:21.000
No way...

18:19.800 --> 18:25.270
But in my country, it's normal to dress 
like this when you go in the water!

18:21.410 --> 18:23.060
I...It can't be...

18:26.000 --> 18:28.510
Th-These are just drawings!

18:28.510 --> 18:30.550
Frighteningly detailed, but still!

18:30.550 --> 18:33.500
A paradise like that could 
never exist in this world!

18:33.500 --> 18:35.690
I'm telling you, it's real!

18:35.690 --> 18:38.970
Just like you see in this photo... 
I mean, picture.

18:39.490 --> 18:42.930
Will you accept that 
I was behaving normally now?

18:42.930 --> 18:45.620
Ah... No, even if that's the case...

18:45.620 --> 18:48.160
W-Well, you've convinced me.

18:48.160 --> 18:51.860
But you really shouldn't 
wear that in this country.

18:51.860 --> 18:53.580
Sh-She's right.

18:53.580 --> 18:56.300
I'll be careful from now on, of course.

18:57.380 --> 19:00.810
Well, now that we've cleared up 
that misunderstanding,

19:01.290 --> 19:03.700
I hope we can work together in the future!

19:03.700 --> 19:04.910
Agreed!

19:04.910 --> 19:05.990
But of course!

19:08.330 --> 19:09.870
Sepp, you, too...

19:09.870 --> 19:11.600
S-Sure...

19:11.600 --> 19:15.090
H-Hey... how much will 
you sell that book for?

19:15.090 --> 19:16.300
It's not for sale!

19:19.010 --> 19:21.160
Thank you for coming!

19:24.860 --> 19:29.950
<i>The lighters and other items I researched 
on that adventure are selling really well!</i>

19:29.950 --> 19:32.400
<i>My savings are slowly increasing...</i>

19:32.820 --> 19:35.770
But slowly is the keyword here!

19:36.650 --> 19:40.360
Is there some way for me 
to rake it in quickly?

19:40.360 --> 19:42.760
That reminds me, that magazine...

19:43.930 --> 19:48.770
No, I won't sell that one because it's 
sure to cause all sorts of headaches...

19:48.770 --> 19:51.300
But what if instead...

19:53.460 --> 19:57.840
No matter the era, art has 
always been necessary to mankind!

19:58.290 --> 19:59.750
Art...

19:59.750 --> 20:01.800
That might not be a bad idea!

20:02.290 --> 20:08.430
<i>But it doesn't feel right to sell copies 
of artwork at high prices, like a con artist...</i>

20:08.990 --> 20:11.740
Create an imitation of 
a piece in the public domain...

20:11.740 --> 20:15.860
Or rather, a transformative derivative work!

20:16.480 --> 20:18.590
I guess that'd be okay...

20:18.590 --> 20:23.570
But I can't draw to save my life, 
or sculpt, either...

20:24.220 --> 20:25.780
Wait, that's it!

20:29.520 --> 20:30.990
Okay, this place should do...

20:32.460 --> 20:34.220
Venus de Milo with arms...

20:34.220 --> 20:37.290
Venus de Milo with arms... C'mon!

20:41.670 --> 20:43.880
You've gotta be kidding!

20:47.340 --> 20:49.670
Nike of Samothrace with a head!

20:49.670 --> 20:51.850
Nike with a head!

20:53.500 --> 20:55.600
Why's she a harpy?

20:56.570 --> 20:59.980
The problem is that I keep thinking 
I have to change something.

20:59.980 --> 21:02.570
Don't think, feel!

21:03.030 --> 21:05.320
A mermaid statue... come on!

21:05.320 --> 21:07.280
Ack!

21:10.350 --> 21:13.710
<i>I can't leave these questionable 
statues in my house,</i>

21:13.710 --> 21:16.270
<i>so I brought them over here 
for the time being.</i>

21:16.710 --> 21:22.550
I forgot I had awful grades in art class, 
as well as arts and crafts...

21:22.550 --> 21:26.190
Although I was good at 
candy-cutting at festivals...

21:27.410 --> 21:28.760
Young miss.

21:28.760 --> 21:29.430
Huh?

21:29.430 --> 21:31.680
Excuse me, but how much 
are you asking for that?

21:32.610 --> 21:33.590
For what?

21:34.560 --> 21:36.610
What fine craftsmanship

21:36.610 --> 21:38.880
these demon statues to ward off evil are!

21:38.880 --> 21:42.180
This hideousness, 
these ghoulish countenances...

21:42.180 --> 21:43.990
Truly spectacular!

21:44.930 --> 21:48.100
<i>I managed to sell it for a pretty good price,</i>

21:48.100 --> 21:52.110
<i>but I'm not happy about it at all!</i>
